From: PLaMo Translate Desktop
Subject: Add the cache_ram_mib load parameter

llama.cpp's server keeps the KV state of earlier prompts in a prompt cache of up to
8192 MiB by default, more than the 4096 MiB of WebAssembly memory: once it grows that far,
allocations fail (std::bad_alloc) and inference aborts. This lets the limit be set, or the
cache disabled with 0, like llama-server's --cache-ram.

